C-style renderer fixtures
=========================

Generate independently against tinygrad a83c6f8011863c17ef4e9c24c59e521be3c754d3:
  python3 packages/tolk/test/golden/cstyle/generate_expected.py \
    --tinygrad _plans/tinygrad-a83c6f801 --output _plans/goldens-a83/cstyle

The explicit output directory permits review before expectations are replaced.
All 78 fixtures invoke the actual target renderer. CUDA/HIP compiler construction
is stubbed because rendering does not compile source; renderer initialization
and matchers run unchanged. No copied HIP renderer matcher remains.

These deliberately ordered linear programs exercise renderer syntax, not the
full lowering pipeline or hardware compilation. Their existing (-1,) parameter
shapes are symbolic render-only names. Required weak CONST sources are inserted
before committed CAST constants, preserving the fixture order and use counts.

Compared with the previous corpus, all 16 Metal files gain the argument-buffer
structure introduced by upstream 277cb9846. Metal/OpenCL/AMD vectorize_index
now exercises an actual committed constant lane index. The old weak literal
was simplified to a scalar load before rendering; it did not test vector lane
syntax. The constructor migration follows the target's inferred-dtype UOp API
and committed constants introduced by 68b4407fe/955037870/a7df1a1ac. Other
expectations remain byte-identical. The generator fails instead of skipping
missing renderers or unsupported fixtures.
